IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — WHAT IS LEFT: the insurer's processing
-- and payment limits, multiple platform operators' insurers, and the
-- administrative and procedural provisions.
--
-- Most of these confer powers on the Commissioner, the Minister or a court,
-- or describe procedure, and compute nothing a case turns on. They are
-- carried here as text, so a reader finds every section, with a few small
-- rules where the Act does fix an answer.
--
-- Source: ../source/WICA2019.txt (sections as cited).

§ `Administration and procedure`

§§ `The insurer pays up to the insured amount (ss 47, 47F; s 18(1))`

-- s 47, s 47F: the insurer "must, in accordance with section 18, pay or
-- deposit that amount, up to the amount insured under that ... insurance
-- policy". s 18(1): a direction to pay is "not exceeding the amount of the
-- employer's liability ... that is insured".
@ref ss 18(1), 47, 47F
GIVEN `the amount ordered` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount insured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the insurer pays of an order of` `the amount ordered` `, insured for` `the amount insured` MEANS
    IF `the amount ordered` GREATER THAN `the amount insured` THEN `the amount insured` ELSE `the amount ordered`

-- s 40: in proceedings on the employer's liability the employer "must provide
-- all reasonable assistance to the employer's insurer"; if it does not, it "is
-- liable to indemnify the employer's insurer for the amount paid or deposited
-- ... under section 18 as a result of the proceedings".
@ref s 40(2)
GIVEN `the employer gave all reasonable assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurer paid`                           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employer's indemnity to its insurer, assistance given:` `the employer gave all reasonable assistance` `, insurer paid` `the insurer paid` MEANS
    IF `the employer gave all reasonable assistance` THEN 0 ELSE `the insurer paid`

§§ `Several platform operators (ss 47A, 47C, 47G)`

-- s 47A(1): the platform operator for processing is the one the worker was
-- serving, or — where several were liable — the one the Commissioner
-- designates by written notice (s 47A(2)).
@ref s 47A
GIVEN `operators served`           IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the operator designated`    IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the relevant platform operator, serving` `operators served` `, designated` `the operator designated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `operators served`
    WHEN only FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF null rest
        THEN only                                                                   -- (1)(a)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the operator designated`
             WHEN JUST o  THEN o                                                    -- (1)(b), (2)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "s 47A(2): the Commissioner has not designated the relevant platform operator"
    WHEN EMPTY THEN REFUSE "s 47A: no platform operator was being served at the time of the accident"

-- s 47C(4)-(5): the relevant PO's insurer pays the whole amount "whether or not
-- that amount exceeds the amount insured". s 47C(6): the other operator's
-- insurer (Y) reimburses "the amount representing the proportion of the
-- compensation payable by Z"; s 47C(7): Z itself, if uninsured. The
-- proportion is s 34E(3)'s (wica-liability.l4).
DECLARE `Reimburser` IS ONE OF
    `the other operator's insurer (Y), s 47C(6)`
    `the other operator itself (Z), s 47C(7)`

@ref s 47C(6)-(7)
GIVEN `Z is insured by a designated PO's insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reimburser`
`who reimburses the relevant PO's insurer, Z insured:` `Z is insured by a designated PO's insurer` MEANS
    IF `Z is insured by a designated PO's insurer`
    THEN `the other operator's insurer (Y), s 47C(6)`
    ELSE `the other operator itself (Z), s 47C(7)`

@ref s 47C(6)-(7)
GIVEN share        IS A NUMBER
      compensation IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reimbursement for a share of` share `of compensation of` compensation MEANS
    compensation TIMES share

-- s 47G(3): recovery "after the later of ... (a) the expiry of the prescribed
-- period starting on the date on which the relevant PO's insurer made payment
-- or deposit ...; (b) where a notice of objection has been given ... — the
-- date on which the Commissioner makes an order under section 47E(9)(b)." The
-- prescribed period is in regulations: its end is an input.
@ref s 47G(3)
GIVEN `the prescribed period ends on` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner's order on`   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day recovery may begin, period ending` `the prescribed period ends on` `, order on` `the Commissioner's order on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Commissioner's order on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the prescribed period ends on`
    WHEN JUST o  THEN IF o GREATER THAN `the prescribed period ends on` THEN o ELSE `the prescribed period ends on`

§§ `Ex gratia payments, enforcement, and the Medical Board`

-- s 70: ex gratia payments from the Workers' Fund of "an amount not exceeding
-- the compensation that [the worker] is entitled to under this Act".
@ref s 70
GIVEN `the ex gratia payment`        IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an ex gratia payment of` `the ex gratia payment` `is within s 70, entitled to` `the compensation entitled to` IF
    `the ex gratia payment` AT MOST `the compensation entitled to`

-- s 21(2)(b)(i): from a deposit, funeral expenses "not exceeding the amount
-- prescribed in regulations made under section 82" — the prescribed amount is
-- an input.
@ref s 21(2)(b)(i)
GIVEN expenses             IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the funeral expenses payable from a deposit, of` expenses `, capped at` `the prescribed cap` MEANS
    IF expenses GREATER THAN `the prescribed cap` THEN `the prescribed cap` ELSE expenses

-- s 60: an order of compensation is enforced by a District Court as its own
-- judgment; "(2) Any sale of immovable property for the purposes of the
-- enforcement may only be ordered by the General Division of the High Court."
@ref s 60(2)
GIVEN `a sale of immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the court that may order the enforcement step, a sale of immovable property:` `a sale of immovable property` MEANS
    IF `a sale of immovable property` THEN "the General Division of the High Court" ELSE "a District Court"

§§ `Carried as text: nothing to compute`

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 1 — short title"
       , "s 5 — purpose of the Act"
       , "s 6 — Assistant Commissioners, investigation officers and authorised persons; delegation"
       , "s 20(2)-(3) — varying a direction to pay relatives; a reasonable opportunity to make representations"
       , "s 21(1), (2)(a)-(e), (3)-(4) — deposit with the Commissioner and the ways of paying it out"
       , "ss 31(1)-(5), (7)-(12), 32, 33 — designation of insurers, conditions, obligations, information"
       , "s 34(2)-(10) — notice, representations, interest and appeal on a designated insurer's penalty"
       , "s 34A — 'work stage 1' and 'work stage 2' (Fifth Schedule Part 1 para 1(3) and Part 2: the stage is an input)"
       , "ss 34B, 34C, 35B — Parts 2, 3 and 4 applied to platform workers: the rules are written once for both"
       , "s 35(2)-(4A) — when an employer or platform operator has notice; the duty to give notice within the prescribed time"
       , "s 35A(1)-(3), (5)-(6) — the Commissioner's directions on processing"
       , "s 36(1) — processing by the employer's insurer"
       , "s 37(2)-(6) — duty to submit to examination; suspension and its lifting"
       , "s 43 — representatives"
       , "ss 44(1)-(4), 45, 47B(1)-(4), 47H — insurers' processing and denial of coverage"
       , "s 47E(4), (6)-(12) — content and effect of platform objections"
       , "s 47I — information for a platform operator's insurer"
       , "s 48(1)-(2), (5)-(6) — notices of assessment"
       , "s 50(1)-(3) — directions by the Commissioner (s 50(4), the offence, is in wica-insurance-offences.l4)"
       , "ss 51(1)-(2), 52, 53, 54(1)-(3), 55, 56 — settlement, pre-hearing conferences, powers and hearings"
       , "s 57 — the Medical Board (its report is conclusive evidence, s 57(5))"
       , "s 58(2)-(4) — procedure on appeal; deposit pending appeal"
       , "s 63(4), (7)-(8) — a reduced order becomes void on suit; the court's certificate"
       , "s 66 — depositions for seafarers"
       , "s 68(1)-(5) — powers of the Commissioner and investigation officers (s 68(6), the offence, is encoded)"
       , "s 69 — reciprocal arrangements"
       , "s 71 — protection from personal liability"
       , "ss 72(1), (4)-(6), 73(1), (4)-(6) — evidence of a body's state of mind; definitions"
       , "ss 74, 75 — the Magistrate and the District Court"
       , "s 78 — immunity for disclosure"
       , "s 79 — exemptions by the Minister"
       , "s 80 — service of documents"
       , "s 81 — amendment of Schedules"
       , "s 82(1)-(2) — regulations (s 82(3)'s ceiling is encoded)"
       , "s 83(2)-(4) — transitional provisions for policies existing on 1 September 2020 (all before the encoded period)"
       , "Fifth Schedule Part 1 para 1 and Part 2 — the definitions of locations and work stages"
